# cursor-text (M13a): the pointer over the page's texts and beside them at 1440 x 900, in the
# default state, with the settings panel open and with a's explainer open: React's `cursor: auto`
# shows the I-beam over a text a press can start a selection in and the arrow beside it, a link the
# pointing hand, and a part that sets a cursor its own (`tools/run view cursor-text` holds the
# port's to WebKit's). Points from the reference's text boxes in WebKit (x, y, width x height;
# .local/probe/m13a/ibeam): the title (213.9, 28.3, 161.4 x 23.5), the subtitle (213.9, 53.5, 275 x
# 14.1), the top bar's empty middle, the wordmark's text (75, 33.9, 97.9 x 28.2; in its link),
# the theme chip's label (1264.5, 39.8, 65.5 x 16.4), "Function" (49, 127, 73.9 x 19.9) and the card
# beside it, the live line's f (53, 231, 8.1 x 28), the form line's gap between ") =" (72.6, 23.4
# wide) and a (104), a's name (93, 415.7, 99.3 x 17.6), its row beside the name, its chip (help),
# P's role (94.4, 682.9, 43.5 x 15.2), P's value (399.8, 678.6, 43.2 x 23.7), P's x (its value
# field), Q's role (97.1, 754.9, 114.7 x 15.2), the Points card between them, the plane and its
# caption (the caption takes no pointer). The settings panel (the gear clicked): "Appearance"
# (1122, 89.2, 87.6 x 13.5), the help line (1122, 156.4, 190.9 x 15.2), an option of the toggle, a
# theme's row, the panel beside its label. a's explainer, opened by ? on a's box (a click types into
# the box, Shift+Tab hands the focus back to it; ? with Shift held, as explainer-key presses it):
# opened by the key it stays as the pointer goes. Its name (542, 425.1, 106.9 x 18.8), the sentence's first line (506, 459.7,
# 245.6 x 17.6), the picture's "a = 2" plate (its a at 725.2, 568.5, 8 x 15) and the picture beside
# it (it takes no pointer: the card's arrow), "In the equation" (506, 696.5, 146.8 x 14.1), the
# gestures' "Drag" (506, 741.4, 28.7 x 15.2) and the card beside the snippet.
